IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `whs-dates`
IMPORT `whs-claims`

-- Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (NSW) -- worked cases for every exported question in whs-claims.l4.
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output. Each
-- assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Dates and amounts are illustrative.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the date`

`in-patient` MEANS `immediate treatment as an in-patient in a hospital`
`amputation` MEANS `immediate treatment for the amputation of any part of the body`
`spinal` MEANS `immediate treatment for a spinal injury`
`lacerations` MEANS `immediate treatment for serious lacerations`
`substance` MEANS `medical treatment after exposure to a substance`
`prescribed injury` MEANS `an injury or illness of a kind the regulations prescribe as serious`
`minor` MEANS `some other treatment, or none`

`fire` MEANS `an uncontrolled implosion, explosion or fire`
`shock` MEANS `electric shock`
`fall of a thing` MEANS `the fall or release from a height of any plant, substance or thing`
`prescribed event` MEANS `another event the regulations prescribe`
`no event` MEANS `none of these events`

`must notify` MEANS `the business must notify the regulator immediately after becoming aware, by the fastest possible means, by telephone or in writing`
`mine` MEANS `no notice is required, because the workplace is one the mines and petroleum sites Act applies to`
`not notifiable` MEANS `no notice is required, because it was not a notifiable incident`
`not of the business` MEANS `no notice is required, because the incident did not arise out of the conduct of the business`

`notify and stay` MEANS `notify the business as soon as practicable that I have ceased work, and remain available to carry out suitable alternative work`
`stay only` MEANS `remain available to carry out suitable alternative work (having ceased on a representative's direction, I need not notify the business)`
`no s 86 duty` MEANS `section 86 puts no duty on me, because I did not cease work under Division 6`

`worker` MEANS `a worker of theirs`
`prospective` MEANS `a prospective worker`
`commercial` MEANS `someone in, or seeking, a commercial arrangement with them`

`hsr` MEANS `I am, have been or propose to be a health and safety representative or committee member`
`raised concern` MEANS `I raise, have raised or propose to raise a work health and safety issue or concern with someone section 106(h) lists`
`sought compliance` MEANS `I am taking, have taken or propose to take action to seek compliance with a duty or obligation under the Act`
`no circumstance` MEANS `none of these reasons`

`discriminated` MEANS `discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason`
`induced` MEANS `requesting, instructing, inducing, encouraging, authorising or assisting discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason`
`coerced` MEANS `coercion or inducement contrary to section 108`
`no conduct` MEANS `none of these kinds of conduct`

`affected` MEANS `I am a person affected by the contravention`
`representative` MEANS `I am a representative authorised by a person affected`
`stranger` MEANS `neither`

`injunction` MEANS `an injunction`
`declaration` MEANS `an order declaring that the person engaged in the conduct`
`compensation` MEANS `an order that the person pay me compensation within a specified period`
`reinstatement` MEANS `an order that I be reinstated or re-employed in my former or a similar position, or employed in the position I applied for or a similar one`
`other order` MEANS `any other order the Industrial Court considers appropriate`

`IM` MEANS `industrial manslaughter (s 34C)`
`cat 1` MEANS `a Category 1 offence (s 31)`
`cat 2` MEANS `a Category 2 offence (s 32)`
`cat 3` MEANS `a Category 3 offence (s 33)`
`s 38(1)` MEANS `failing to notify a notifiable incident (s 38(1))`
`s 38(7)` MEANS `failing to keep the record of a notifiable incident (s 38(7))`
`s 39` MEANS `failing to preserve an incident site (s 39(1))`
`s 104` MEANS `discriminatory conduct, or requesting or assisting it (s 104 or 107)`
`s 108` MEANS `coercion or inducement (s 108)`
`s 109` MEANS `misrepresentation about rights under the Act (s 109)`
`s 273` MEANS `levying a worker for health and safety (s 273)`

`PCBU` MEANS `an individual conducting the business or undertaking, or an officer of it`
`individual` MEANS `any other individual`
`company` MEANS `a body corporate`

`indictment` MEANS `on indictment`
`summary` MEANS `summarily, before the Local Court or the Industrial Court`
`summary unless elected` MEANS `summarily, before the Local Court or the Industrial Court, unless the prosecutor elects to proceed on indictment`

`in time` MEANS `done in time`
`late` MEANS `done late`
`overdue` MEANS `not done, and the time has passed`
`still open` MEANS `not done yet, and the time has not passed`
`not required` MEANS `no time limit applies, because it was not required`

§§ `s 7 -- am I a worker`

-- Arguments: work for a business; conduct it and work in it; police officer.
#ASSERT `Am I a worker` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a worker` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a worker` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a worker` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 5 -- business or undertaking`

-- Arguments: conducts a business; volunteer association; elected council member; solely a worker or officer.
#ASSERT `Is the one I work for a person conducting a business or undertaking` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the one I work for a person conducting a business or undertaking` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the one I work for a person conducting a business or undertaking` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the one I work for a person conducting a business or undertaking` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the one I work for a person conducting a business or undertaking` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 36 -- serious injury or illness`

-- Arguments: treatment; hours from exposure to medical treatment; regulations exclude.
#ASSERT `Is my injury or illness a serious injury or illness` `in-patient` 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my injury or illness a serious injury or illness` `amputation` 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my injury or illness a serious injury or illness` `spinal` 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my injury or illness a serious injury or illness` `lacerations` 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my injury or illness a serious injury or illness` `prescribed injury` 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "within 48 hours of exposure to a substance": the 48th hour is in, 48.5 is out.
#ASSERT `Is my injury or illness a serious injury or illness` `substance` 47 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my injury or illness a serious injury or illness` `substance` 48 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my injury or illness a serious injury or illness` `substance` 48.5 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my injury or illness a serious injury or illness` `minor` 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "does not include an illness or injury of a prescribed kind".
#ASSERT `Is my injury or illness a serious injury or illness` `in-patient` 0 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 37 -- dangerous incident`

-- Arguments: what it involved; serious risk from immediate or imminent exposure; regulations exclude.
#ASSERT `Was it a dangerous incident` `fire` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was it a dangerous incident` `shock` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was it a dangerous incident` `prescribed event` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was it a dangerous incident` `fall of a thing` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was it a dangerous incident` `no event` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was it a dangerous incident` `fire` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 35, 38(1), 38(8) -- must the business notify`

-- Arguments: died; treatment; hours; injury excluded; incident kind; serious risk; incident excluded; arose out of the
-- business; mine or petroleum site.
#ASSERT `Must the business notify the regulator` TRUE `minor` 0 FALSE `no event` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `must notify`
#ASSERT `Must the business notify the regulator` FALSE `in-patient` 0 FALSE `no event` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `must notify`
#ASSERT `Must the business notify the regulator` FALSE `minor` 0 FALSE `fire` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `must notify`
#ASSERT `Must the business notify the regulator` FALSE `substance` 60 FALSE `no event` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not notifiable`
#ASSERT `Must the business notify the regulator` FALSE `minor` 0 FALSE `no event` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not notifiable`
#ASSERT `Must the business notify the regulator` FALSE `in-patient` 0 FALSE `no event` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not of the business`
#ASSERT `Must the business notify the regulator` TRUE `minor` 0 FALSE `no event` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `mine`

§§ `s 38(4)(b) -- written notice within 48 hours`

-- Arguments: written notice required; given; hours to the notice; hours since the requirement.
#ASSERT `Was the written notice of my incident given in time` TRUE TRUE 20 60 EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Was the written notice of my incident given in time` TRUE TRUE 48 60 EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Was the written notice of my incident given in time` TRUE TRUE 49 60 EQUALS `late`
#ASSERT `Was the written notice of my incident given in time` TRUE FALSE 0 30 EQUALS `still open`
#ASSERT `Was the written notice of my incident given in time` TRUE FALSE 0 48 EQUALS `still open`
#ASSERT `Was the written notice of my incident given in time` TRUE FALSE 0 50 EQUALS `overdue`
#ASSERT `Was the written notice of my incident given in time` FALSE FALSE 0 100 EQUALS `not required`

