§§ `s 231(2) -- the regulator's answer within 3 months`

-- Arguments: day received; advised; day advised; today. 30 November 2025 plus three months is 28 February 2026.
#ASSERT `Has the regulator answered my request in time` (`d` 30 11 2025) TRUE (`d` 15 1 2026) (`d` 1 4 2026) EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Has the regulator answered my request in time` (`d` 30 11 2025) TRUE (`d` 28 2 2026) (`d` 1 4 2026) EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Has the regulator answered my request in time` (`d` 30 11 2025) TRUE (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 1 4 2026) EQUALS `late`
#ASSERT `Has the regulator answered my request in time` (`d` 30 11 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 28 2 2026) EQUALS `still open`
#ASSERT `Has the regulator answered my request in time` (`d` 30 11 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 3 2026) EQUALS `overdue`

§§ `s 231(3)(b), (4) -- referral to the Director of Public Prosecutions`

#ASSERT `By what day must the regulator refer my matter to the DPP` (`d` 31 1 2026) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2026
#ASSERT `By what day must the regulator refer my matter to the DPP` (`d` 10 3 2026) EQUALS `d` 10 4 2026
#ASSERT `By what day must the DPP advise the regulator` (`d` 31 3 2026) EQUALS `d` 30 4 2026
#ASSERT `By what day must the DPP advise the regulator` (`d` 15 12 2026) EQUALS `d` 15 1 2027

§§ `ss 232, 34E -- the limitation period for the prosecution`

-- Arguments: offence; regulator knew; coroner showed an offence; coroner's day; undertaking contravened or withdrawn;
-- its latest day; fresh evidence for Category 1; today.
-- Two years after the regulator knew.
#ASSERT `By what day must a prosecution be brought` `cat 2` (`d` 10 1 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `the prosecution must be brought by` (`d` 10 1 2027)
-- The inquest ended 1 June 2026: a year after is later.
#ASSERT `By what day must a prosecution be brought` `cat 2` (`d` 10 1 2025) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `the prosecution must be brought by` (`d` 1 6 2027)
-- An inquest that ended early: the regulator's two years are later.
#ASSERT `By what day must a prosecution be brought` `cat 2` (`d` 10 1 2025) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `the prosecution must be brought by` (`d` 10 1 2027)
-- The undertaking contravened 1 March 2027: six months after is the latest.
#ASSERT `By what day must a prosecution be brought` `cat 3` (`d` 10 1 2025) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2026) TRUE (`d` 1 3 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `the prosecution must be brought by` (`d` 1 9 2027)
-- Industrial manslaughter: no limit.
#ASSERT `By what day must a prosecution be brought` `IM` (`d` 10 1 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2030) EQUALS `there is no time limit, because it is industrial manslaughter`
-- Category 1 with fresh evidence, after the period: still possible; before the period ends: the ordinary last day.
#ASSERT `By what day must a prosecution be brought` `cat 1` (`d` 10 1 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) TRUE (`d` 11 1 2027) EQUALS `the period has ended, but a Category 1 prosecution may still be brought on fresh evidence the court accepts`
#ASSERT `By what day must a prosecution be brought` `cat 1` (`d` 10 1 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) TRUE (`d` 10 1 2027) EQUALS `the prosecution must be brought by` (`d` 10 1 2027)
-- Fresh evidence does not help a Category 2 prosecution.
#ASSERT `By what day must a prosecution be brought` `cat 2` (`d` 10 1 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) TRUE (`d` 11 1 2027) EQUALS `the prosecution must be brought by` (`d` 10 1 2027)

§§ `s 267 -- a right to sue under the Act`

#ASSERT `Does this Act give me a right to sue for the breach` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does this Act give me a right to sue for the breach` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 272 -- contracting out`

#ASSERT `Is this term of my contract void` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this term of my contract void` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

